Integrate close into algebraize, per-rule

Structure exposes an equate(a, b, conflicts) method that declares two
elements equal. It unifies their equivalence classes and merges their
concrete-type entries (propagating along parents of matching types)
but does not run the functionality/typing fixed point. close() is
still the caller's job.

algebraize wires this up for IfAtom::Equal, ThenAtom::Equal and the
`var := term` form of ThenAtom::Defined. build_structures now
accumulates a Vec<TypeConflict> alongside Structures and returns both.

Rule processing is one rule at a time: walk the rule body (which
pushes rule_initial plus every stmt's before/after into the arena),
then close every structure produced during that walk before moving on
to the next rule.

close() switched to a sink-style `conflicts: &mut Vec<TypeConflict>`
parameter to match equate().

Structure carries an eqlog_runtime::Unification<ElId> tracking
equality between elements, and els is a BTreeMap<ElId,
Option<ConcreteType>> where ConcreteType pairs a non-optional TypeId
with its parent-model elements. After close, only equivalence-class
roots remain as els keys and every FuncApp, PredApp, var-el value and
ConcreteType.parents reference points at a canonical root.
